  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Is an executive MBA worth it in India? Only for one specific profile: a senior
    professional who already holds real leadership scope and wants to accelerate that path, not
    reinvent it.</strong>
    An executive MBA (EMBA) is not a scheduling variant of a regular MBA. It is a different product
    built for a different problem — working professionals with roughly 5-10+ years of experience,
    running on a weekend or modular format so you keep your salary and your job while you study.
    If your real goal is a full career pivot into a new industry or function, a regular full-time
    MBA usually serves that goal better than an EMBA does. Used on the right profile, at the right
    stage, it is a genuine lever toward a bigger income ceiling and earlier financial freedom; used
    on the wrong profile, it is an expensive credential that adds a title without adding real scope.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li>An EMBA is built for professionals with roughly 5-10+ years of experience who already have real leadership scope — a team, a budget, or a function — and want to accelerate that trajectory without pausing income.</li>
      <li>Format is weekend or modular over 12-18 months, not full-time and on-campus like a regular MBA. Fees at established Indian programs commonly run Rs 15-40 lakh; ISB's flagship program runs close to Rs 37 lakh.</li>
      <li>If your real goal is a career pivot into a new industry or function, a regular full-time MBA usually serves that goal better — EMBA cohorts and recruiter relationships are built to deepen an existing path, not launch a new one.</li>
      <li>Employer sponsorship is real but not guaranteed: globally only about a quarter of EMBA candidates get full funding, so have the sponsorship conversation with your employer before you apply.</li>
      <li>Do not take a large personal loan for a credential that offers no campus placement reset. The value should appear inside your current trajectory through broader scope, stronger leadership proof, a promotion path, or employer funding.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

