            <td data-label="Tier"><strong>{item.tier}</strong></td>
            <td data-label="What to expect">{item.signal}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Regardless of tier, the same due-diligence question applies: ask for the last two years of
    participant outcomes for people in a role and industry close to yours, not a generic placement
    headline. A program that cannot show you recent, specific outcomes is telling you something
    important through that silence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">Use The 4-Checkpoint Protocol before you apply</h2>

  <p>
    A strong brand name or an appealing salary-growth statistic cannot tell you whether an EMBA
    fits your specific situation. The 4-Checkpoint Protocol narrows the decision to what actually
    matters for you.
  </p>

  <div class="protocol-stack">
    {checkpointItems.map((item) => (
      <div class="checkpoint">
        <div class="checkpoint__num">{item.num}</div>
        <div class="checkpoint__body">
